  "limits": "This search needs an object to be seen as a point of light in at least three visits (5 times the noise in two of them and 4 times in a third), to stay inside the picture in all of them, and to be clear of bright stars and of catalogued infrared sources. It cannot find anything in a field with fewer than three visits, anything that changes brightness a lot from visit to visit, or an object so near that it smears within a visit (the table gives the limit at each distance). Catalogues built from ten years of WISE data reach fainter than one SPHEREx visit at these wavelengths, so finding nothing is the expected answer.",
